• Affected Facilities: Second-Floor Reading Hall, Print Catalog Terminals, and Mobile App Borrowing
• Book Return Drop-Box: Remains open 24 hours at the East Courtyard entrance

Due dates for all borrowed physical books falling between December 1 and December 3 will be automatically extended to Monday, December 7 without late fines. Printed newspapers will remain accessible inside the ground-floor lobby cafe from 8:00 AM to 4:00 PM. Inquiries may be directed to support@civiclibrary.org.', 'Why is Civic Public Library temporarily closing the Second-Floor Reading Hall and e-book portal?', '[{"key":"A","text":"To upgrade Wi-Fi routers to fiber-optic speed and migrate the reservation system."},{"key":"B","text":"To clean water damage caused by a burst roof pipe above the print terminals."},{"key":"C","text":"To host a three-day community book auction in the East Courtyard."},{"key":"D","text":"To replace all printed newspapers with digital tablets before January."},{"key":"E","text":"To renovate the ground-floor lobby cafe and add seating areas."}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Read the opening sentence of the notice to library members.', 'The closure is scheduled "to install faster fiber-optic Wi-Fi routers and migrate our book reservation database."', ARRAY['announcement', 'detail', 'library']::text[]),
