• Team Composition: 2–3 students accompanied by one certified science mentor
• Prizes: National research grants worth IDR 45,000,000 and full sponsorship for top two teams to attend the Tokyo Youth Science Symposium

All projects must include a three-minute demonstration video and an original data logbook verified by the school principal. Late entries submitted after March 5 will not be reviewed by the jury panel. Apply online at youthsif.id.', 'Who is eligible to enter projects in the Archipelago Youth Science & Innovation Fair 2027?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Undergraduate engineering students at Indonesian public universities."},{"key":"B","text":"Solo middle school inventors competing without teacher supervision."},{"key":"C","text":"Any adult resident residing in Jakarta who submits an essay by March 10."},{"key":"D","text":"Science teachers submitting commercial patents developed in Tokyo."},{"key":"E","text":"Teams of two or three high school students in Grades 10–12 guided by a certified mentor."}]'::jsonb, 'E', 'Combine the introductory invitation with the second bullet point.', 'The call invites high school students in Grades 10–12 forming teams of 2–3 students with one certified science mentor.', ARRAY['announcement', 'detail', 'science-fair']::text[]),
