MERIT SCHOLARSHIP FOR CLEAN ENERGY ENGINEERING TRACK

Applications are now open for ten full-tuition fellowships supporting outstanding high school seniors entering the Undergraduate Clean Energy & Hydrology Track.

• Award Coverage: 100% four-year tuition waiver, campus dormitory housing, and an annual laboratory book allowance
• Academic Eligibility: Minimum cumulative grade average of 88/100 in Mathematics and Physics, plus English proficiency equivalent to B2 (IELTS 6.0)
• Selection Timeline: Shortlisted applicants will complete an online problem-solving interview on May 12

Interested candidates must upload two recommendation letters and a 600-word essay proposing a practical solar or water-conservation solution for their home district by April 25. Incomplete files cannot be considered.', 'Which financial benefits are included in the Clean Energy Engineering fellowship?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Full four-year tuition, campus dormitory housing, and an annual lab book allowance."},{"key":"B","text":"A 50% tuition reduction paired with free laptop repairs."},{"key":"C","text":"Guaranteed paid internships in Stockholm without academic grade rules."},{"key":"D","text":"Only a one-semester discount on off-campus apartment rentals."},{"key":"E","text":"Monthly cash stipends strictly for international airline tickets."}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Check the first bullet point labeled "Award Coverage."', 'The fellowship covers a 100% four-year tuition waiver, campus dormitory housing, and an annual laboratory book allowance.', ARRAY['announcement', 'detail', 'scholarship']::text[]),
