Walk-in donors are welcome, though booking a 30-minute time slot via harapancare.org/donate helps eliminate waiting time. Please bring a valid national ID or student ID card and eat a light meal beforehand.', 'Who among the following individuals fails to meet the stated eligibility requirements to donate blood?', '[{"key":"A","text":"A 17-year-old student weighing 52 kg who slept 7 hours and ate breakfast."},{"key":"B","text":"A 58-year-old nurse weighing 60 kg bringing her official ID card."},{"key":"C","text":"A 45-year-old parent weighing 65 kg who rested 6 hours and had light toast."},{"key":"D","text":"A 24-year-old engineer weighing 45 kg who booked a 9:00 AM slot online."},{"key":"E","text":"A 30-year-old teacher weighing 55 kg arriving as a walk-in with her national ID."}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Compare each candidate’s age, weight ("at least 48 kg"), and sleep against the requirements.', 'Donors must weigh at least 48 kg; a person weighing 45 kg does not meet the minimum weight criterion.', ARRAY['announcement', 'application', 'hospital']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-AN-024', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'announcements', 'Announcements & Service Advisories', 'medium', 'C2', 'announcement', 'HARAPAN COMMUNITY HOSPITAL — WEEKEND BLOOD DONATION & HEALTH CHECK DRIVE

Be a Lifesaver This Saturday!

Harapan Community Hospital, together with the Regional Red Cross Unit, invites healthy community members to join our semi-annual blood donation campaign to replenish city hospital reserves before the holiday travel season.

• Date & Venue: Saturday, December 12, 2026 | 8:30 AM – 2:30 PM | Hospital West Wing Atrium
• Donor Requirements: Aged 17–60 years, body weight at least 48 kg, and well rested (minimum 5 hours of sleep)
• Complimentary Benefits: Free blood pressure screening, iron-level check, nutritious recovery meal box, and a digital donor badge

Walk-in donors are welcome, though booking a 30-minute time slot via harapancare.org/donate helps eliminate waiting time. Please bring a valid national ID or student ID card and eat a light meal beforehand.', 'What advantage does pre-booking a 30-minute time slot online offer donors?', '[{"key":"A","text":"It enables nurses to collect donations directly at the donor’s home."},{"key":"B","text":"It lowers the minimum body weight rule to 42 kilograms."},{"key":"C","text":"It waives the requirement to carry an identification card."},{"key":"D","text":"It prevents donors from having to wait long at the venue."},{"key":"E","text":"It doubles the number of recovery meal boxes handed out."}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Read the opening sentence of the final paragraph.', 'Although walk-ins are welcome, booking a slot via the link "helps eliminate waiting time."', ARRAY['announcement', 'detail', 'hospital']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-AN-025', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'announcements', 'Announcements & Service Advisories', 'mudah', 'C2', 'announcement', 'METROPOLITAN WATER WORKS — SCHEDULED PIPELINE FLUSHING & PRESSURE TEST

Customer Advisory for Southern District Neighborhoods:

To maintain safe drinking water quality, technicians will perform high-pressure sediment flushing across main underground supply lines next Monday night.

• Maintenance Window: Monday, November 30, 11:00 PM through Tuesday, December 1, 4:30 AM
• Impacted Areas: Sukajaya, Taman Mawar, and Kebon Agung blocks 1–12
• Expected Impact: Temporary drop in tap water pressure or brief cloudy appearance immediately after service restoration

We advise households to store enough clean water in advance for nighttime use. Once service resumes at 4:30 AM, let cold-water faucets run for two to three minutes until the water clears completely before running washing machines. Emergency water tankers can be requested via 1500-288.', 'Why is Metropolitan Water Works conducting maintenance from late Monday night until early Tuesday morning?', '[{"key":"A","text":"To install new residential electric water heaters before December."},{"key":"B","text":"To shut off water permanently across Taman Mawar blocks 1–12."},{"key":"C","text":"To repair a broken surface bridge inside Kebon Agung."},{"key":"D","text":"To flush underground supply pipes and protect drinking water quality."},{"key":"E","text":"To sell emergency water tankers to commercial laundromats."}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Read the opening sentence of the customer advisory.', 'Technicians are performing high-pressure sediment flushing across underground supply lines "to maintain safe drinking water quality."', ARRAY['announcement', 'detail', 'utilities']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-AN-026', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'announcements', 'Announcements & Service Advisories', 'medium', 'C3', 'announcement', 'METROPOLITAN WATER WORKS — SCHEDULED PIPELINE FLUSHING & PRESSURE TEST

Customer Advisory for Southern District Neighborhoods:

To maintain safe drinking water quality, technicians will perform high-pressure sediment flushing across main underground supply lines next Monday night.

• Maintenance Window: Monday, November 30, 11:00 PM through Tuesday, December 1, 4:30 AM
• Impacted Areas: Sukajaya, Taman Mawar, and Kebon Agung blocks 1–12
• Expected Impact: Temporary drop in tap water pressure or brief cloudy appearance immediately after service restoration

We advise households to store enough clean water in advance for nighttime use. Once service resumes at 4:30 AM, let cold-water faucets run for two to three minutes until the water clears completely before running washing machines. Emergency water tankers can be requested via 1500-288.', 'What precaution should residents in impacted blocks take right after water service resumes at 4:30 AM before using washing machines?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Run cold-water taps for two to three minutes until the water clears completely."},{"key":"B","text":"Drain all hot water tanks and call 1500-288 immediately."},{"key":"C","text":"Keep all faucets tightly shut for twenty-four hours to preserve pressure."},{"key":"D","text":"Wait until 11:00 PM Tuesday night before opening any kitchen faucet."},{"key":"E","text":"Boil every liter of laundry water before pouring it into the machine."}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Check the instruction in the second sentence of the last paragraph.', 'Because temporary cloudiness may appear right after restoration, customers are told to "let cold-water faucets run for two to three minutes until the water clears completely before running washing machines."', ARRAY['announcement', 'application', 'utilities']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-AN-027', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'announcements', 'Announcements & Service Advisories', 'sulit', 'C4', 'announcement', 'METROPOLITAN WATER WORKS — SCHEDULED PIPELINE FLUSHING & PRESSURE TEST

Customer Advisory for Southern District Neighborhoods:

To maintain safe drinking water quality, technicians will perform high-pressure sediment flushing across main underground supply lines next Monday night.

• Maintenance Window: Monday, November 30, 11:00 PM through Tuesday, December 1, 4:30 AM
• Impacted Areas: Sukajaya, Taman Mawar, and Kebon Agung blocks 1–12
• Expected Impact: Temporary drop in tap water pressure or brief cloudy appearance immediately after service restoration

We advise households to store enough clean water in advance for nighttime use. Once service resumes at 4:30 AM, let cold-water faucets run for two to three minutes until the water clears completely before running washing machines. Emergency water tankers can be requested via 1500-288.', 'Which combination of three facts is stated in the Water Works advisory?
(1) Flushing runs for 5.5 hours overnight from November 30 to December 1.
(2) Only commercial factories in Northern District will notice lower pressure.
(3) Households are recommended to store adequate clean water before 11:00 PM.
(4) Tap water may briefly look cloudy right after restoration.
(5) Residents must pay an extra surcharge if they request an emergency water tanker.', '[{"key":"A","text":"Statements (1), (2), and (3)"},{"key":"B","text":"Statements (3), (4), and (5)"},{"key":"C","text":"Statements (1), (4), and (5)"},{"key":"D","text":"Statements (1), (3), and (4)"},{"key":"E","text":"Statements (2), (4), and (5)"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Verify the exact time window (11:00 PM to 4:30 AM = 5.5 hours) and affected neighborhoods (Southern District).', '11:00 PM to 4:30 AM is 5.5 hours (1); storing clean water is advised (3); brief cloudy appearance may happen (4). Southern District households are impacted (not Northern factories), and no tanker surcharge is mentioned.', ARRAY['announcement', 'complex-mcq', 'hots']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-AN-028', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'announcements', 'Announcements & Service Advisories', 'mudah', 'C2', 'announcement', 'CODECRAFT BOOTCAMP × ZURICH SOFTWARE POLYTECHNIC

LAUNCHING THE APPLIED CYBERSECURITY CERTIFICATE-TO-DIPLOMA BRIDGE

Experienced IT practitioners and vocational school graduates can now convert hands-on security credentials into an accredited European Applied Diploma without quitting their day jobs.

• Accelerated Track: Complete 4 specialized lab modules in 9 months rather than the standard 18 months
• Assessment Format: Real-time simulated network defense labs and peer code audits—zero timed multiple-choice midterms
• Program Cost: CHF 1,450 per term, including virtual cloud-lab server access and an optional 0% employer sponsorship invoice plan

Graduates receive dual verification credentials recognized across partner firms in Europe and Southeast Asia. Enrollment for the Winter Cohort closes January 10. Explore the syllabus at codecraft.io/zurich.', 'How long does the accelerated Applied Cybersecurity Diploma bridge take compared with the standard schedule?', '[{"key":"A","text":"12 months instead of 24 months."},{"key":"B","text":"18 months instead of 36 months."},{"key":"C","text":"9 months instead of 18 months."},{"key":"D","text":"24 months instead of 48 months."},{"key":"E","text":"4 months instead of 9 months."}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'Check the first bullet point ("Accelerated Track").', 'Participants "complete 4 specialized lab modules in 9 months rather than the standard 18 months."', ARRAY['announcement', 'detail', 'cybersecurity']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-AN-029', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'announcements', 'Announcements & Service Advisories', 'medium', 'C3', 'announcement', 'CODECRAFT BOOTCAMP × ZURICH SOFTWARE POLYTECHNIC

LAUNCHING THE APPLIED CYBERSECURITY CERTIFICATE-TO-DIPLOMA BRIDGE

Experienced IT practitioners and vocational school graduates can now convert hands-on security credentials into an accredited European Applied Diploma without quitting their day jobs.

• Accelerated Track: Complete 4 specialized lab modules in 9 months rather than the standard 18 months
• Assessment Format: Real-time simulated network defense labs and peer code audits—zero timed multiple-choice midterms
• Program Cost: CHF 1,450 per term, including virtual cloud-lab server access and an optional 0% employer sponsorship invoice plan

Graduates receive dual verification credentials recognized across partner firms in Europe and Southeast Asia. Enrollment for the Winter Cohort closes January 10. Explore the syllabus at codecraft.io/zurich.', 'What kind of evaluation method replaces traditional timed multiple-choice midterms in this program?', '[{"key":"A","text":"In-person oral defenses held exclusively at Zurich airport lounges."},{"key":"B","text":"Live simulated network defense labs and peer code audits."},{"key":"C","text":"Weekly vocabulary quizzes conducted without server access."},{"key":"D","text":"Handwritten essays graded twice a year on European history."},{"key":"E","text":"Unpaid full-time summer apprenticeships requiring job resignation."}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Look at the second bullet point labeled "Assessment Format."', 'Students are assessed through "real-time simulated network defense labs and peer code audits" with zero timed multiple-choice midterms.', ARRAY['announcement', 'detail', 'cybersecurity']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-AN-030', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'announcements', 'Announcements & Service Advisories', 'sulit', 'C4', 'announcement', 'CODECRAFT BOOTCAMP × ZURICH SOFTWARE POLYTECHNIC

LAUNCHING THE APPLIED CYBERSECURITY CERTIFICATE-TO-DIPLOMA BRIDGE

Experienced IT practitioners and vocational school graduates can now convert hands-on security credentials into an accredited European Applied Diploma without quitting their day jobs.

• Accelerated Track: Complete 4 specialized lab modules in 9 months rather than the standard 18 months
• Assessment Format: Real-time simulated network defense labs and peer code audits—zero timed multiple-choice midterms
• Program Cost: CHF 1,450 per term, including virtual cloud-lab server access and an optional 0% employer sponsorship invoice plan

Graduates receive dual verification credentials recognized across partner firms in Europe and Southeast Asia. Enrollment for the Winter Cohort closes January 10. Explore the syllabus at codecraft.io/zurich.', 'Which combination of three details accurately summarizes the CodeCraft × Zurich announcement?
(1) Working IT staff must resign from their current jobs to enroll.
(2) Tuition of CHF 1,450 per term covers virtual cloud-lab server access.
(3) Employers may sponsor tuition through an optional 0% installment/invoice plan.
(4) Applications for the Winter Cohort close on January 10.
(5) Certificates are valid solely inside Swiss municipal offices.', '[{"key":"A","text":"Statements (1), (2), and (4)"},{"key":"B","text":"Statements (1), (3), and (5)"},{"key":"C","text":"Statements (2), (3), and (4)"},{"key":"D","text":"Statements (3), (4), and (5)"},{"key":"E","text":"Statements (2), (4), and (5)"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'Check "without quitting their day jobs" and "recognized across partner firms in Europe and Southeast Asia."', 'Statements (2), (3), and (4) are explicitly confirmed in the bullet points and closing paragraph.', ARRAY['announcement', 'complex-mcq', 'hots']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-001', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'mudah', 'C2', 'text', 'Chess is an ancient strategy board game that challenges players to think critically and plan several moves ahead. Unlike games based purely on luck, it requires deep concentration and tactical foresight. Beginners usually learn how individual pieces move, while experienced players study complex opening strategies and endgame patterns. Its intellectual depth has enabled the game to thrive across cultures for centuries.', 'The paragraph contains several verbs, including ….', '[{"key":"A","text":"strategy, moves, study"},{"key":"B","text":"ancient, tactical, complex"},{"key":"C","text":"critically, purely, usually"},{"key":"D","text":"concentration, individual, patterns"},{"key":"E","text":"challenges, learn, thrive"}]'::jsonb, 'E', 'Identify words showing actions or processes rather than nouns, adjectives, or -ly adverbs.', '"Challenges" (predicate of the relative clause), "learn" (main verb for beginners), and "thrive" (to-infinitive verb) are all verbs; the other sets mix nouns, adjectives, and adverbs.', ARRAY['parts-of-speech', 'verbs', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-002', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'mudah', 'C2', 'text', 'The Apollo 11 mission represents one of the greatest achievements in human exploration. Launched in July 1969 by NASA, the spacecraft carried three astronauts toward the Moon. Its success fulfilled a historic goal and inspired future generations of scientists, engineers, and researchers. The mission is remembered for its precision, technological innovation, and iconic figures, such as Neil Armstrong and Buzz Aldrin. Decades later, Apollo 11 remains a symbol of human curiosity.', 'The paragraph contains several nouns, including ….', '[{"key":"A","text":"launched, carried, inspired"},{"key":"B","text":"represents, remembered, remains"},{"key":"C","text":"human, iconic, technological"},{"key":"D","text":"mission, precision, curiosity"},{"key":"E","text":"greatest, historic, future"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Look for abstract and concrete naming words often preceded by "the," "its," or an adjective.', '"Mission," "precision," and "curiosity" function as nouns in the paragraph. The remaining options contain adjectives or verbs.', ARRAY['parts-of-speech', 'nouns', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-003', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'Kyoto is a historic Japanese … famous for its classical Buddhist temples and traditional wooden houses. It has preserved cultural treasures such as Kinkaku-ji, Fushimi Inari Shrine, and the Arashiyama Bamboo Grove. Many visitors admire its atmosphere of serenity, …, and timeless beauty. The city is especially celebrated for its seasonal cherry blossoms and … tea ceremonies. Its heritage continues to attract travelers from every corner of the globe.', 'Fill in the blanks with the correct part of speech!', '[{"key":"A","text":"city – elegantly – authenticity"},{"key":"B","text":"city – elegance – authentic"},{"key":"C","text":"city – elegant – authenticity"},{"key":"D","text":"civic – elegance – authentic"},{"key":"E","text":"citizen – elegant – authentically"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Check the structure: noun (a historic Japanese ___), parallel noun (serenity, ___, beauty), and adjective (___ tea ceremonies).', 'Blank 1 requires a noun referring to Kyoto ("city"); blank 2 must match the nouns "serenity" and "beauty" ("elegance"); blank 3 modifies the noun phrase "tea ceremonies" ("authentic").', ARRAY['parts-of-speech', 'word-formation', 'cloze', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-004', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'Komodo dragons are giant lizards … to a few volcanic islands in eastern Indonesia. They inhabit dry savannas and tropical forests, where they hunt prey using their keen sense of smell. These reptiles play a vital role as apex predators by maintaining balance in their local ecosystems. However, climate change and habitat fragmentation … their long-term survival. Strict conservation laws, ecotourism management, and habitat monitoring are … to protect this rare species.', 'Fill in the blanks with the correct part of speech!', '[{"key":"A","text":"endemically – danger – crucially"},{"key":"B","text":"endemic – dangerous – crucial"},{"key":"C","text":"endemic – endanger – crucial"},{"key":"D","text":"endemically – endanger – cruciality"},{"key":"E","text":"endemism – endanger – crucial"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'Blank 1 needs an adjective modifying "giant lizards," blank 2 needs a plural verb, and blank 3 follows the linking verb "are."', '"Endemic" (adjective) describes where they naturally belong; "endanger" (verb) is the action of the plural subject; "crucial" (adjective) completes the linking verb "are."', ARRAY['parts-of-speech', 'word-formation', 'cloze', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-005', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'mudah', 'C2', 'text', 'The science laboratory contains sensitive chemical equipment and glassware. Students … eat, drink, or run inside the lab under any circumstances. However, once the teacher gives instructions, you … begin conducting the experiment with your lab partner. Always wear your safety goggles properly.', 'The correct modal verbs to complete the paragraph are ….', '[{"key":"A","text":"could not – might"},{"key":"B","text":"must not – may"},{"key":"C","text":"may not – will"},{"key":"D","text":"cannot – should"},{"key":"E","text":"should not – must"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Notice strict prohibition ("under any circumstances") followed by polite permission once instructions are given.', '"Must not" expresses strict prohibition against eating or running in a lab, while "may" grants formal permission after teacher instructions.', ARRAY['modals', 'prohibition', 'permission', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-006', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'Strong winds are blowing from the coast, and the sea waves are rising rapidly. The ferry service … be delayed this afternoon if the storm intensifies. If the coast guard issues a red warning, all boat trips … be canceled immediately for passenger safety.', 'The correct modal verbs to complete the paragraph are ….', '[{"key":"A","text":"may – will"},{"key":"B","text":"can – must"},{"key":"C","text":"could – ought to"},{"key":"D","text":"must – should"},{"key":"E","text":"should – can"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'The first condition indicates future possibility ("if the storm intensifies"), while the second states a definite automatic safety outcome.', '"May" fits real possibility ("may be delayed"), and "will" states a certain real-conditional result when a red warning is issued ("all boat trips will be canceled").', ARRAY['modals', 'possibility', 'prediction', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-007', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'mudah', 'C2', 'text', 'Speaking confidently in front of a large audience takes regular practice. Two years ago, I … deliver a short speech without trembling nervously. Now, after joining the school debate club, I … present complex arguments clearly and calmly.', 'The correct modal verbs to complete the paragraph are ….', '[{"key":"A","text":"will not – should"},{"key":"B","text":"could not – can"},{"key":"C","text":"cannot – will"},{"key":"D","text":"should not – could"},{"key":"E","text":"must not – may"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Compare past inability ("Two years ago") against present ability ("Now").', '"Could not" shows lack of ability two years ago, and "can" expresses current ability gained through debate club practice.', ARRAY['modals', 'ability', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-008', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'Volunteering at the local animal shelter is a great way to help the community. You … choose whether you want to walk the dogs or clean the cat enclosures. Once you finish your shift, … you please sign the attendance log at the front desk? Thank you for your kindness!', 'The correct modal verbs to complete the paragraph are ….', '[{"key":"A","text":"could – may"},{"key":"B","text":"should – could"},{"key":"C","text":"must – can"},{"key":"D","text":"can – should"},{"key":"E","text":"may – will"}]'::jsonb, 'E', 'Look for permission/option first, followed by the polite request marker "... you please sign".', '"May" offers an option/permission ("You may choose..."), and "will" fits a polite request paired with "please" ("will you please sign...").', ARRAY['modals', 'permission', 'request', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-009', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'mudah', 'C2', 'text', 'Protecting your digital privacy is crucial in today''s connected world. Internet users … share their home addresses or passwords with strangers on social media. Instead, you … enable two-factor authentication to keep your personal accounts secure.', 'The correct modal verbs to complete the paragraph are ….', '[{"key":"A","text":"cannot – should"},{"key":"B","text":"should not – must"},{"key":"C","text":"may not – will"},{"key":"D","text":"must not – can"},{"key":"E","text":"could not – may"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'First comes safety advice against a bad habit ("... share addresses with strangers"), followed by an essential security rule.', '"Should not" gives strong warning advice against oversharing personal data, and "must" stresses the necessity of enabling two-factor authentication.', ARRAY['modals', 'advice', 'necessity', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-010', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'sulit', 'C4', 'text', 'Complete these three sentences with the correct derivatives of the word CREATE:
1. Modern wind turbines … clean electricity for thousands of coastal homes.
2. Brainstorming in small groups is a great way to spark … ideas.
3. This handcrafted ceramic vase is the artist’s finest … to date.', 'Which sequence accurately completes sentences (1), (2), and (3)?', '[{"key":"A","text":"creatively – creation – creative"},{"key":"B","text":"create – creativity – creatively"},{"key":"C","text":"create – creative – creation"},{"key":"D","text":"creative – creativity – creation"},{"key":"E","text":"creation – creative – create"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'Match sentence 1 (plural verb), sentence 2 (adjective before "ideas"), and sentence 3 (singular noun after "finest").', '"Create" is the verb after "turbines"; "creative" is the adjective describing "ideas"; "creation" is the noun meaning an artwork.', ARRAY['word-formation', 'matching-adapted', 'hots', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-011', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'Complete these two sentences with the correct derivatives of the word CREATE:
1. Art classes play an important role in nurturing student ….
2. She solved the packaging problem … by using biodegradable bamboo.', 'Which word pair accurately completes sentences (1) and (2)?', '[{"key":"A","text":"creative – creativity"},{"key":"B","text":"creativity – creatively"},{"key":"C","text":"creatively – create"},{"key":"D","text":"creation – creative"},{"key":"E","text":"create – creation"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Blank 1 needs an uncountable noun ("the quality of being imaginative"), while blank 2 needs an adverb modifying "solved."', '"Creativity" (noun) fits the compound phrase "student creativity," and "creatively" (adverb) explains how she solved the packaging problem.', ARRAY['word-formation', 'matching-adapted', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-012', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'Choose the appropriate modal verbs for sentences (1)–(3):
1. All laboratory visitors … wear protective eyewear before entering the room.
2. The renovated city museum … open its doors to the public next Tuesday.
3. Penguins … fly through the air despite having wings and feathers.', 'Which sequence correctly completes sentences (1), (2), and (3)?', '[{"key":"A","text":"will – cannot – may"},{"key":"B","text":"cannot – must – will"},{"key":"C","text":"should not – may – cannot"},{"key":"D","text":"may – should not – must"},{"key":"E","text":"must – will – cannot"}]'::jsonb, 'E', 'Identify safety obligation ("protective eyewear"), definite future schedule ("next Tuesday"), and physical impossibility.', '"Must" signals mandatory lab safety, "will" expresses a scheduled future opening, and "cannot" states biological inability.', ARRAY['modals', 'matching-adapted', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-013', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'mudah', 'C2', 'text', 'Choose the appropriate modal verbs for sentences (1) and (2):
1. Passengers … board the aircraft once their zone number is announced.
2. You … stare at bright computer screens right before going to sleep.', 'Which pair correctly completes both sentences?', '[{"key":"A","text":"may – should not"},{"key":"B","text":"must – may"},{"key":"C","text":"will – cannot"},{"key":"D","text":"should not – must"},{"key":"E","text":"cannot – will"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Sentence 1 expresses official permission to board; sentence 2 offers healthy sleep advice.', '"May" expresses formal permission at the boarding gate, whereas "should not" advises against harmful screen exposure at bedtime.', ARRAY['modals', 'matching-adapted', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-014', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'sulit', 'C4', 'none', NULL, 'Which pair of sentences uses both "succeed" (verb) and "success" (noun) accurately and meaningfully?', '[{"key":"A","text":"If we practice daily, we can success together. / Everyone admired the succeed of the concert."},{"key":"B","text":"She is very succeed in science. / Their project made a strong succeeded yesterday."},{"key":"C","text":"You will achieve succeed if you study consistently. / Hard work helps you to success every final exam."},{"key":"D","text":"You must work hard if you want to succeed in your career. / Teamwork was the main key to our success in the debate tournament."},{"key":"E","text":"Succeeding is our biggest success goal tomorrow. / They worked hard so they could successful."}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Check that "succeed" follows "to" or a modal as a base verb, while "success" sits after a determiner/preposition as a noun.', 'In "want to succeed," "succeed" is properly used as a verb after "to"; in "to our success," "success" correctly functions as a noun after the possessive "our."', ARRAY['parts-of-speech', 'word-formation', 'writing-adapted', 'hots', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-015', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'mudah', 'C2', 'text', 'Tropical mangrove forests shield vulnerable coastlines from destructive ocean waves. Their dense underwater roots filter muddy runoff and trap carbon efficiently inside coastal sediment. Biologists frequently survey these wetlands to monitor crab populations and protect nesting birds.', 'Which group from the paragraph consists solely of verbs?', '[{"key":"A","text":"mangrove, runoff, sediment"},{"key":"B","text":"efficiently, frequently, coastal"},{"key":"C","text":"shield, filter, trap"},{"key":"D","text":"wetlands, biologists, populations"},{"key":"E","text":"vulnerable, destructive, dense"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'Focus on the action words performed by "mangrove forests" and "roots."', '"Shield" (protect), "filter" (clean), and "trap" (capture) all act as transitive verbs with direct objects.', ARRAY['parts-of-speech', 'verbs']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-016', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'mudah', 'C2', 'text', 'Modern radio telescopes capture faint electromagnetic signals from distant galaxies. Astronomers store enormous datasets on high-speed servers before analyzing cosmic patterns. International collaboration strengthens our understanding of stellar evolution.', 'Which list contains only nouns taken from the paragraph?', '[{"key":"A","text":"faint, distant, enormous"},{"key":"B","text":"capture, store, strengthens"},{"key":"C","text":"signals, datasets, evolution"},{"key":"D","text":"modern, cosmic, international"},{"key":"E","text":"before, from, analyzing"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'Identify names of things/concepts that appear after adjectives or prepositions.', '"Signals," "datasets," and "evolution" are all nouns; the other groups hold verbs, adjectives, or prepositions.', ARRAY['parts-of-speech', 'nouns']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-017', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'medium', 'C2', 'text', 'A symphony orchestra requires remarkable discipline from every young musician. Talented violinists follow rapid tempo shifts while attentive percussionists count silent measures. Together, they deliver an unforgettable live performance.', 'Which group from the paragraph contains strictly adjectives?', '[{"key":"A","text":"together, while, every"},{"key":"B","text":"orchestra, shifts, measures"},{"key":"C","text":"discipline, musician, performance"},{"key":"D","text":"remarkable, talented, unforgettable"},{"key":"E","text":"requires, follow, count"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Look for descriptive words directly modifying nouns such as "discipline," "violinists," and "performance."', '"Remarkable" modifies "discipline," "talented" modifies "violinists," and "unforgettable" modifies "performance"—all three are adjectives.', ARRAY['parts-of-speech', 'adjectives']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-018', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'During hazardous mountain rescues, paramedics quickly assess injured climbers and speak calmly to keep everyone focused. Pilots maneuver rescue helicopters carefully through swirling fog, rarely canceling critical flights unless visibility drops completely.', 'Which word list consists entirely of adverbs found in the paragraph?', '[{"key":"A","text":"rescue, focused, swirling"},{"key":"B","text":"hazardous, injured, critical"},{"key":"C","text":"quickly, calmly, carefully"},{"key":"D","text":"assess, speak, maneuver"},{"key":"E","text":"climbers, fog, visibility"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'Look for words modifying how verbs ("assess," "speak," "maneuver") are performed.', '"Quickly" modifies "assess," "calmly" modifies "speak," and "carefully" modifies "maneuver"—all function as adverbs of manner.', ARRAY['parts-of-speech', 'adverbs']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-019', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'Green startups across Southeast Asia continually … smart irrigation sensors for smallholder farms. Their … approach reduces freshwater waste by nearly forty percent. Universities often partner with founders to accelerate technological … in rural agriculture.', 'Fill in the blanks with the correct derivatives of INNOVATE!', '[{"key":"A","text":"innovate – innovative – innovation"},{"key":"B","text":"innovator – innovation – innovate"},{"key":"C","text":"innovate – innovatively – innovative"},{"key":"D","text":"innovative – innovatively – innovation"},{"key":"E","text":"innovation – innovative – innovate"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Identify the needed forms in order: plural verb after "startups," adjective before "approach," and noun after "technological."', '"Innovate" is the present plural verb; "innovative" modifies the noun "approach"; "innovation" serves as the noun object of "accelerate."', ARRAY['word-formation', 'cloze']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-020', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'Wildlife sanctuaries in Kalimantan work closely with village cooperatives to … endangered orangutan habitats. Long-term … depends on preventing illegal logging and forest fires. Even students can contribute … by avoiding products linked to deforestation.', 'Fill in the blanks with the correct derivatives of CONSERVE / RESPONSIBLE!', '[{"key":"A","text":"conserve – conservative – responsibility"},{"key":"B","text":"conservation – conserve – responsible"},{"key":"C","text":"conserving – conservation – responsibility"},{"key":"D","text":"conserve – conservation – responsibly"},{"key":"E","text":"conservative – conserve – responsibly"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Notice "to + V1" in blank 1, a noun subject ("Long-term ___") in blank 2, and a manner adverb modifying "contribute" in blank 3.', 'After "to" we use base verb "conserve"; the subject of "depends" is the noun "conservation"; and the adverb "responsibly" modifies "contribute."', ARRAY['word-formation', 'cloze']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-021', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'sulit', 'C4', 'text', 'Accessible quality … empowers young citizens to participate meaningfully in civic life. Community libraries now host interactive workshops designed to … teenagers about financial literacy. Moreover, well-designed … software makes mathematics engaging for visual learners.', 'Fill in the blanks with the correct derivatives of EDUCATE!', '[{"key":"A","text":"education – educate – educational"},{"key":"B","text":"education – educated – educationally"},{"key":"C","text":"educator – education – educated"},{"key":"D","text":"educate – educational – education"},{"key":"E","text":"educational – education – educate"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Check blank 1 (noun phrase "Accessible quality ___"), blank 2 ("designed to + V1"), and blank 3 (adjective modifying "software").', '"Education" completes the noun subject; "to educate" supplies the infinitive verb; and "educational" modifies "software."', ARRAY['word-formation', 'cloze', 'hots']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-022', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'Batik artisans in Solo preserve cultural … handed down across countless generations. Every … geometric motif carries philosophical meaning tied to family harmony. Ceremonial textiles are … worn during weddings and formal national celebrations.', 'Fill in the blanks with the correct derivatives of TRADITION!', '[{"key":"A","text":"traditions – traditional – traditionally"},{"key":"B","text":"traditional – traditionally – traditions"},{"key":"C","text":"tradition – traditionally – traditional"},{"key":"D","text":"traditional – traditions – tradition"},{"key":"E","text":"traditionally – tradition – traditional"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Look at plural noun ("cultural ___"), adjective before "motif," and adverb before passive verb "worn."', '"Traditions" (noun) receives "preserve"; "traditional" (adjective) describes "geometric motif"; and "traditionally" (adverb) modifies "are worn."', ARRAY['word-formation', 'cloze']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-023', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'sulit', 'C4', 'text', 'Architectural planners increasingly design … public buildings powered by rooftop solar arrays. Urban forests help … cooler microclimates during scorching dry seasons. Ultimately, long-term environmental … requires everyday cooperation between municipalities and households.', 'Fill in the blanks with the correct derivatives of SUSTAIN!', '[{"key":"A","text":"sustain – sustainable – sustainability"},{"key":"B","text":"sustainably – sustaining – sustainable"},{"key":"C","text":"sustainable – sustain – sustainability"},{"key":"D","text":"sustainable – sustainability – sustain"},{"key":"E","text":"sustainability – sustain – sustainable"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'Trace adjective ("___ public buildings"), bare infinitive verb after "help," and abstract noun subject ("environmental ___").', '"Sustainable" (adjective) modifies "public buildings"; "sustain" (verb after "help") means maintain; "sustainability" (noun) functions as the subject of "requires."', ARRAY['word-formation', 'cloze', 'hots']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-024', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'sulit', 'C4', 'text', 'High-speed rail corridors stimulate regional … growth by linking port cities with industrial hubs. Solar-powered cold storage facilities are … viable for small fishing cooperatives. Strengthening rural … helps young entrepreneurs remain in their hometowns.', 'Fill in the blanks with the correct derivatives of ECONOMY!', '[{"key":"A","text":"economy – economic – economically"},{"key":"B","text":"economics – economically – economic"},{"key":"C","text":"economical – economies – economy"},{"key":"D","text":"economic – economically – economies"},{"key":"E","text":"economically – economy – economic"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Distinguish "economic growth" (relating to the economy), the adverb before adjective "viable," and plural noun after "rural."', '"Economic" is the adjective modifying "growth"; "economically" is the adverb modifying "viable"; and "economies" is the plural noun after "rural."', ARRAY['word-formation', 'cloze', 'hots']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-025', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'Mentors can deeply … students by sharing honest stories about overcoming academic setbacks. Watching her elder brother complete a marathon became the … for Maya’s own daily training routine. Her determination offered an … example to everyone on the track team.', 'Fill in the blanks with the correct derivatives of INSPIRE!', '[{"key":"A","text":"inspire – inspiring – inspiration"},{"key":"B","text":"inspiration – inspire – inspired"},{"key":"C","text":"inspiring – inspiration – inspire"},{"key":"D","text":"inspired – inspire – inspirationally"},{"key":"E","text":"inspire – inspiration – inspiring"}]'::jsonb, 'E', 'Look for base verb after modal "can," noun after "the," and participial adjective before "example."', '"Inspire" follows modal "can"; "inspiration" serves as the noun after "the"; and "inspiring" describes the "example" (an example that inspires others).', ARRAY['word-formation', 'cloze']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-026', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'mudah', 'C2', 'text', 'Firefighters risk their lives whenever alarms ring at night. Visitors … block emergency fire exits with backpacks or bicycles in school hallways. During an earthquake drill, everyone … stay calm and follow teacher directions to the assembly field.', 'The correct modal verbs to complete the paragraph are ….', '[{"key":"A","text":"could not – might"},{"key":"B","text":"might not – can"},{"key":"C","text":"would not – may"},{"key":"D","text":"must not – must"},{"key":"E","text":"will not – could"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Both blanks describe strict safety rules: one prohibition and one mandatory emergency procedure.', '"Must not" prohibits blocking fire exits, and "must" expresses the obligation to remain calm and evacuate safely.', ARRAY['modals', 'obligation', 'prohibition']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-027', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'mudah', 'C2', 'text', 'Learning conversational Mandarin takes steady daily listening. Six months ago, Naufal … recognize even twenty basic characters. Today, after practicing flashcards every evening, he … read short restaurant menus effortlessly.', 'The correct modal verbs to complete the paragraph are ….', '[{"key":"A","text":"should not – may"},{"key":"B","text":"cannot – could"},{"key":"C","text":"could not – can"},{"key":"D","text":"must not – should"},{"key":"E","text":"may not – will"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'Contrast past ability ("Six months ago") against present ability ("Today").', '"Could not" marks inability six months ago, and "can" highlights current reading capability.', ARRAY['modals', 'ability']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-028', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'Dark gray clouds are gathering swiftly over Mount Merbabu before midday. The hiking guide warns that heavy fog … roll over the ridge within an hour. Therefore, climbers … pack waterproof jackets before leaving basecamp.', 'The correct modal verbs to complete the paragraph are ….', '[{"key":"A","text":"will not – must"},{"key":"B","text":"might – should"},{"key":"C","text":"must – may not"},{"key":"D","text":"would – ought not"},{"key":"E","text":"can – cannot"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Combine weather uncertainty/possibility in blank 1 with practical safety advice in blank 2.', '"Might" expresses an uncertain weather possibility, and "should" provides sensible preparation advice.', ARRAY['modals', 'possibility', 'advice']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-029', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'When using a crowded public Wi-Fi hotspot at a café, students … enter sensitive banking PIN numbers without a secure encrypted connection. Instead, you … wait until you reach home or use mobile cellular data for private transactions.', 'The correct modal verbs to complete the paragraph are ….', '[{"key":"A","text":"will not – might"},{"key":"B","text":"must – must not"},{"key":"C","text":"cannot – would"},{"key":"D","text":"may – could not"},{"key":"E","text":"should not – ought to"}]'::jsonb, 'E', 'Look for negative advice first followed by an equivalent alternative recommendation using "ought to."', '"Should not" warns against risky banking on open Wi-Fi, while "ought to" recommends a safer alternative.', ARRAY['modals', 'advice']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-030', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'Excuse me, receptionist: my parents are waiting outside the exhibition gate with digital passes. … they enter the main hall through Side Entrance B, or … they line up at the front ticket desk first?', 'The correct modal verbs to complete the inquiry are ….', '[{"key":"A","text":"May – must"},{"key":"B","text":"Must – cannot"},{"key":"C","text":"Should – will not"},{"key":"D","text":"Will not – should not"},{"key":"E","text":"Might not – could not"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'First ask politely for permission ("... they enter"), then ask about mandatory procedure ("or ... they line up").', '"May they enter..." asks politely for permission, while "must they line up..." asks whether standing at the ticket desk is mandatory.', ARRAY['modals', 'permission', 'obligation']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-031', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'sulit', 'C4', 'text', 'No lights are glowing inside the auditorium, and the front entrance door is padlocked with a "Closed for Cleaning" sign. The drama rehearsal … be taking place in there right now; the cast members … have moved to the music room upstairs.', 'Which modal pair accurately expresses strong logical deduction in the paragraph?', '[{"key":"A","text":"will – may not"},{"key":"B","text":"cannot – must"},{"key":"C","text":"must – cannot"},{"key":"D","text":"should – must not"},{"key":"E","text":"might – would not"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Use "cannot" for logical impossibility (dark/padlocked hall) and "must (have)" for strong logical certainty.', 'Because the auditorium is dark and padlocked, rehearsal logically "cannot" be inside; therefore, the cast "must" have relocated upstairs.', ARRAY['modals', 'deduction', 'hots']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-032', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'Every participant in the school marathon … submit a signed medical clearance form by Thursday afternoon. However, volunteers handing out water cups along the track … bring medical forms since they are not running the race.', 'The correct modal verbs to complete the rule are ….', '[{"key":"A","text":"may not – must not"},{"key":"B","text":"do not have to – must"},{"key":"C","text":"could – cannot"},{"key":"D","text":"should not – might"},{"key":"E","text":"must – do not have to"}]'::jsonb, 'E', 'Contrast mandatory obligation ("must") against absence of necessity ("do not have to").', 'Runners are required ("must") to provide medical clearance, while non-running volunteers face no requirement ("do not have to").', ARRAY['modals', 'obligation', 'lack-of-necessity']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-033', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'sulit', 'C4', 'text', 'Mrs. Tanu looks exhausted at her desk after grading ninety essays overnight. Even though she prefers drinking black coffee, … you bring her a bottle of cool mineral water instead? You … ask the assistant first so you do not interrupt her phone call.', 'The correct modal verbs to complete the paragraph are ….', '[{"key":"A","text":"must – may not"},{"key":"B","text":"might – cannot"},{"key":"C","text":"should not – will"},{"key":"D","text":"shall – must not"},{"key":"E","text":"could – should"}]'::jsonb, 'E', 'First is a courteous request ("___ you bring...?"), followed by polite thoughtful advice.', '"Could you bring..." forms a polite request, and "should" advises checking with the assistant courteously.', ARRAY['modals', 'request', 'advice', 'hots']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-034', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'Our badminton coach has already booked Court 3 for Saturday morning, so we … reserve another court elsewhere. Still, every player … arrive fifteen minutes early for stretching.', 'The correct modal verbs to complete the paragraph are ….', '[{"key":"A","text":"need not – should"},{"key":"B","text":"must not – can not"},{"key":"C","text":"cannot – may not"},{"key":"D","text":"might – would not"},{"key":"E","text":"must – could not"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Because Court 3 is already booked, booking another court is unnecessary ("need not").', '"Need not" expresses lack of necessity ("do not need to reserve another court"), while "should" gives the warm-up expectation.', ARRAY['modals', 'lack-of-necessity', 'advice']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-PM-035', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'parts-of-speech-modals', 'Parts of Speech, Word Forms & Modal Verbs', 'sulit', 'C4', 'text', 'Although Daniel practiced hard yesterday, he realized he … finish assembling the science display alone before dusk. Fortunately, he asked two classmates to stay, and together they … complete the project smoothly by 5:00 PM.', 'Which modal pair fits both past negative inability and general past achievement?', '[{"key":"A","text":"may not – might"},{"key":"B","text":"will not – could not"},{"key":"C","text":"must not – should"},{"key":"D","text":"could not – were able to"},{"key":"E","text":"cannot – can"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Remember: for a single specific past achievement after overcoming difficulty ("completed by 5:00 PM yesterday"), "were able to" is preferred over affirmative "could."', '"Could not" describes Daniel’s past inability working alone, and "were able to" properly captures succeeding on a specific past occasion.', ARRAY['modals', 'past-ability', 'hots']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-VT-001', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'verb-tenses', 'Verb Tenses (Present, Past & Perfect)', 'mudah', 'C2', 'none', NULL, 'Fill in the blank with the correct verb!
Every winter, thousands of monarch butterflies … across North America to reach warmer regions.', '[{"key":"A","text":"are migrating"},{"key":"B","text":"have migrated"},{"key":"C","text":"migrates"},{"key":"D","text":"migrate"},{"key":"E","text":"were migrating"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Look at the recurring time marker "Every winter" and the plural subject "thousands of monarch butterflies."', '"Every winter" expresses a regular recurring seasonal fact (Simple Present). Because the subject "thousands of monarch butterflies" is plural, use the base verb "migrate."', ARRAY['verb-tenses', 'simple-present', 'phb-tenses']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-VT-002', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'verb-tenses', 'Verb Tenses (Present, Past & Perfect)', 'mudah', 'C2', 'none', NULL, 'Fill in the blank with the correct verb!
Look! That street artist … a realistic portrait of a famous football player right in front of us.', '[{"key":"A","text":"painted"},{"key":"B","text":"is painting"},{"key":"C","text":"had painted"},{"key":"D","text":"paints"},{"key":"E","text":"has painted"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '"Look!" and "right in front of us" signal an action happening at this exact moment.', 'Exclamations like "Look!" combined with "right in front of us" require Present Continuous: "is painting."', ARRAY['verb-tenses', 'present-continuous', 'phb-tenses']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-VT-003', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'verb-tenses', 'Verb Tenses (Present, Past & Perfect)', 'mudah', 'C2', 'none', NULL, 'Fill in the blank with the correct verb!
Scientists … several unusual creatures in the deepest parts of the ocean so far.', '[{"key":"A","text":"has discovered"},{"key":"B","text":"have discovered"},{"key":"C","text":"had discovered"},{"key":"D","text":"discover"},{"key":"E","text":"discovered"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Note the time expression "so far" up to the present and the plural subject "Scientists."', '"So far" denotes actions accomplished up to now (Present Perfect), and plural "Scientists" pairs with "have discovered."', ARRAY['verb-tenses', 'present-perfect', 'phb-tenses']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-VT-004', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'verb-tenses', 'Verb Tenses (Present, Past & Perfect)', 'mudah', 'C2', 'none', NULL, 'Fill in the blank with the correct verb!
Last Saturday, my friends and I … an abandoned railway station during our photography trip.', '[{"key":"A","text":"were exploring"},{"key":"B","text":"are exploring"},{"key":"C","text":"have explored"},{"key":"D","text":"explored"},{"key":"E","text":"explore"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '"Last Saturday" specifies a finished point in past time.', 'A definite finished past time marker ("Last Saturday") takes Simple Past Tense: "explored."', ARRAY['verb-tenses', 'simple-past', 'phb-tenses']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-VT-005', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'verb-tenses', 'Verb Tenses (Present, Past & Perfect)', 'medium', 'C3', 'none', NULL, 'Fill in the blank with the correct verb!
At exactly midnight yesterday, the security guard … the museum when he heard a strange noise.', '[{"key":"A","text":"is patrolling"},{"key":"B","text":"patrolled"},{"key":"C","text":"has patrolled"},{"key":"D","text":"had patrolled"},{"key":"E","text":"was patrolling"}]'::jsonb, 'E', 'An ongoing action at a specific past time ("At exactly midnight yesterday") was interrupted by "when he heard."', 'Past Continuous ("was patrolling") describes the background action in progress at midnight yesterday when the noise occurred.', ARRAY['verb-tenses', 'past-continuous', 'phb-tenses']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-VT-006', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'verb-tenses', 'Verb Tenses (Present, Past & Perfect)', 'medium', 'C3', 'none', NULL, 'Fill in the blank with the correct verb!
By the time the rescue helicopter arrived, the hikers … their emergency supplies.', '[{"key":"A","text":"use"},{"key":"B","text":"used"},{"key":"C","text":"have used"},{"key":"D","text":"had used"},{"key":"E","text":"are using"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Notice "By the time + Simple Past (arrived)" — which action happened earlier?', '"By the time" with a past event triggers Past Perfect ("had used") for the earlier completed action.', ARRAY['verb-tenses', 'past-perfect', 'phb-tenses']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-VT-007', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'verb-tenses', 'Verb Tenses (Present, Past & Perfect)', 'mudah', 'C2', 'none', NULL, 'Fill in the blank with the correct verb!
Clarine usually … animated movies whenever she has free time.', '[{"key":"A","text":"has watched"},{"key":"B","text":"watches"},{"key":"C","text":"watched"},{"key":"D","text":"is watching"},{"key":"E","text":"watch"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Adverb "usually" and singular third-person subject "Clarine" point to habitual present.', 'Simple Present with third-person singular "Clarine" takes -es ending: "watches."', ARRAY['verb-tenses', 'simple-present', 'phb-tenses']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-VT-008', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'verb-tenses', 'Verb Tenses (Present, Past & Perfect)', 'medium', 'C3', 'none', NULL, 'Fill in the blank with the correct verb!
Penelope … presenting her thesis defense when I entered the room.', '[{"key":"A","text":"finished"},{"key":"B","text":"has finished"},{"key":"C","text":"had finished"},{"key":"D","text":"finishes"},{"key":"E","text":"have finished"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'Expressing that the defense was already completed prior to the moment "I entered the room."', 'Past Perfect ("had finished") indicates Penelope completed presenting before the second past event ("when I entered").', ARRAY['verb-tenses', 'past-perfect', 'phb-tenses']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-VT-009', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'verb-tenses', 'Verb Tenses (Present, Past & Perfect)', 'mudah', 'C2', 'none', NULL, 'Fill in the blank with the correct verb!
Hubert … three international photography competitions since he joined the photography club.', '[{"key":"A","text":"is entering"},{"key":"B","text":"enters"},{"key":"C","text":"has entered"},{"key":"D","text":"entered"},{"key":"E","text":"have entered"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '"Since + past event (he joined)" connects a past starting point up to the present.', 'Use Present Perfect ("has entered" for singular Hubert) to express cumulative experiences since a past point ("since he joined").', ARRAY['verb-tenses', 'present-perfect', 'phb-tenses']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-VT-010', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'verb-tenses', 'Verb Tenses (Present, Past & Perfect)', 'mudah', 'C2', 'none', NULL, 'Fill in the blank with the correct verb!
The famous explorer … a hidden waterfall during his expedition in the Amazon rainforest in 2022.', '[{"key":"A","text":"finds"},{"key":"B","text":"had found"},{"key":"C","text":"has found"},{"key":"D","text":"found"},{"key":"E","text":"is finding"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Specific finished year "in 2022" requires simple past tense.', 'Whenever a closed past year ("in 2022") is specified, use Simple Past Tense ("found").', ARRAY['verb-tenses', 'simple-past', 'phb-tenses']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-VT-011', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'verb-tenses', 'Verb Tenses (Present, Past & Perfect)', 'medium', 'C3', 'none', NULL, 'Fill in the blanks with the correct verbs!
