  ('ENG10-RS-025', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'sulit', 'C4', 'none', NULL, 'Read the sentence carefully!
Ryan explained that he had been decorating the classroom at exactly 3 p.m. the previous day.
Change the reported speech above into a direct speech!', '[{"key":"A","text":"Ryan explained, “I was decorating the classroom at exactly 3 p.m. the day before.”"},{"key":"B","text":"Ryan explained, “I was decorating the classroom at exactly 3 p.m. yesterday.”"},{"key":"C","text":"Ryan explained, “I had been decorating the classroom at exactly 3 p.m. yesterday.”"},{"key":"D","text":"Ryan explained, “I have been decorating the classroom at exactly 3 p.m. yesterday.”"},{"key":"E","text":"Ryan explained, “I had been decorating the classroom at exactly 3 p.m. the day before.”"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Remember: Past Continuous + specific past time ("at 3 p.m. yesterday") backshifts to Past Perfect Continuous when reported.', 'Because "at exactly 3 p.m. yesterday" anchors an ongoing past point, the original direct quote used Past Continuous ("I was decorating ... at exactly 3 p.m. yesterday").', ARRAY['reported-to-direct', 'hots', 'phb-reported']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-026', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'sulit', 'C4', 'none', NULL, 'Read the sentence carefully!
Tery asked Cynthia if she had tried the new Italian restaurant over there the previous week.
Change the reported speech above into a direct speech!', '[{"key":"A","text":"Tery asked Cynthia, “Did you tried the new Italian restaurant over here last week?”"},{"key":"B","text":"Tery asked Cynthia, “Do you try the new Italian restaurant over here last week?”"},{"key":"C","text":"Tery asked Cynthia, “Had you tried the new Italian restaurant over here the previous week?”"},{"key":"D","text":"Tery asked Cynthia, “Have you tried the new Italian restaurant over here last week?”"},{"key":"E","text":"Tery asked Cynthia, “Did you try the new Italian restaurant over here last week?”"}]'::jsonb, 'E', 'Reverse "she had tried + over there + the previous week" back into an accurate Simple Past question with "you," "over here," and "last week."', 'In direct speech, "last week" cannot pair with Present Perfect ("Have you tried"); thus it must be Simple Past ("Did you try ... over here last week?").', ARRAY['reported-to-direct', 'yes-no-question', 'hots', 'phb-reported']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-027', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'sulit', 'C4', 'none', NULL, 'Read the sentence carefully!
Emma wonders whether Noel would join the English club next semester.
Change the reported speech above into a direct speech!', '[{"key":"A","text":"Emma wonders, “Noel, would you join the English club next semester?”"},{"key":"B","text":"Emma wonders, “Noel, would I join the English club next semester?”"},{"key":"C","text":"Emma wonders, “Noel, will I join the English club next semester?”"},{"key":"D","text":"Emma wonders, “Noel, would you join the English club the following semester?”"},{"key":"E","text":"Emma wonders, “Noel, will you join the English club next semester?”"}]'::jsonb, 'A', '"Emma wonders" is Present Tense (so no backshift occurred from direct to reported!). Therefore "would" was already "would" in direct speech, and "next semester" stayed "next semester."', 'Since "wonders" is in the present tense, neither modal nor time shifted during reporting; the original direct question asked Noel politely using "would you join ... next semester?".', ARRAY['reported-to-direct', 'present-reporting', 'hots', 'phb-reported']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-028', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'sulit', 'C4', 'none', NULL, 'Read the sentence carefully!
Glenn wanted to know why Amanda hadn''t submitted her application by then.
Change the reported speech above into a direct speech!', '[{"key":"A","text":"Glenn wanted to know, “Why haven’t you submitted her application by then, Amanda?”"},{"key":"B","text":"Glenn wanted to know, “Why hadn’t she submitted her application by then, Amanda?”"},{"key":"C","text":"Glenn wanted to know, “Why you hadn’t submitted your application by now, Amanda?”"},{"key":"D","text":"Glenn wanted to know, “Why hadn’t you submitted your application by now, Amanda?”"},{"key":"E","text":"Glenn wanted to know, “Why haven’t you submitted your application by now, Amanda?”"}]'::jsonb, 'E', 'Reverse "hadn''t submitted ... by then" -> Present Perfect ("haven''t submitted ... by now") and switch "her -> your."', '"By now" signals Present Perfect in direct speech ("Why haven’t you submitted your application by now, Amanda?"), which backshifted to "hadn’t submitted ... by then" under "wanted."', ARRAY['reported-to-direct', 'wh-question', 'hots', 'phb-reported']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-029', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'sulit', 'C5', 'none', NULL, 'Read the sentence carefully!
Grace has been wondering why the photographer hadn''t published those pictures before the journalist arrived.
Change the reported speech above into a direct speech!', '[{"key":"A","text":"Grace has been wondering, “Why the photographer hadn’t published those pictures before the journalist arrived?”"},{"key":"B","text":"Grace has been wondering, “Why hasn’t the photographer published these pictures before the journalist arrives?”"},{"key":"C","text":"Grace has been wondering, “Why hadn’t the photographer published those pictures before the journalist had arrived?”"},{"key":"D","text":"Grace has been wondering, “Why hadn’t the photographer published those pictures before the journalist arrived?”"},{"key":"E","text":"Grace has been wondering, “Why didn’t the photographer publish those pictures before the journalist arrives?”"}]'::jsonb, 'D', '"Has been wondering" is Present Perfect (a present reporting tense!), so no backshift took place; restore WH-question inversion ("Why hadn''t the photographer...?").', 'With present-time reporting ("has been wondering"), tenses do not change; we simply revert indirect statement order back to inverted question order ("Why hadn’t the photographer published... before the journalist arrived?").', ARRAY['reported-to-direct', 'present-reporting', 'hots', 'phb-reported']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-030', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'mudah', 'C2', 'none', NULL, 'Read the sentence carefully!
The librarian told the students not to make noise in the reading room.
Change the reported speech above into a direct speech!', '[{"key":"A","text":"The librarian told the students, “You don’t make noise in the reading room.”"},{"key":"B","text":"The librarian tells the students, “Don’t make noise in the reading room.”"},{"key":"C","text":"The librarian told the students, “Don’t making noise in the reading room.”"},{"key":"D","text":"The librarian told the students, “Make noise in the reading room.”"},{"key":"E","text":"The librarian told the students, “Don’t make noise in the reading room.”"}]'::jsonb, 'E', 'Keep past reporting verb "told" and turn "not to make noise" back into a negative imperative.', '"Not to make noise" restores cleanly to the direct negative command "Don’t make noise in the reading room." while preserving "told."', ARRAY['reported-to-direct', 'negative-imperative', 'phb-reported']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-031', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'Daniel said, "I am designing a mobile app for our school project because I want to help students organize their schedules."', 'Change the direct speech above into reported speech!', '[{"key":"A","text":"Daniel said that he was designing a mobile app for their school project because I wanted to help students organize their schedules."},{"key":"B","text":"Daniel said that he had designed a mobile app for our school project because he wanted to help students organize their schedules."},{"key":"C","text":"Daniel said that he had been designing a mobile app for our school project because he wanted to help students organize their schedules."},{"key":"D","text":"Daniel said that he was designing a mobile app for their school project because he wanted to help students organize their schedules."},{"key":"E","text":"Daniel said that he was designing a mobile app for their school project because he had wanted to help students organize their schedules."}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Check all shifts together: "I -> he", "am designing -> was designing", "our -> their", and "want -> wanted."', 'Under past "said," Present Continuous ("am designing") shifts to "was designing," Simple Present ("want") shifts to "wanted," and "I/our" adjust to "he/their."', ARRAY['reported-speech', 'pronoun-shift', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-032', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'Nadia asks me, "Where did you find this rare vintage book yesterday?"', 'Change the direct speech above into reported speech!', '[{"key":"A","text":"Nadia asked where I found that rare vintage book the day before."},{"key":"B","text":"Nadia asked where I had found that rare vintage book the previous day."},{"key":"C","text":"Nadia asks where did I find that rare vintage book yesterday."},{"key":"D","text":"Nadia asks where I found that rare vintage book yesterday."},{"key":"E","text":"Nadia asks where I had found this rare vintage book yesterday."}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Notice Present Tense reporting verb "asks" (keep reporting verb in present and retain Simple Past "found" + "yesterday"), while removing question auxiliary "did."', 'Because "asks" is Present Tense, tense does not backshift ("did you find" -> "I found", "yesterday" remains), while "did" drops and statement order is used.', ARRAY['reported-speech', 'present-reporting', 'wh-question', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-033', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'Coach Ryan asked his players, "Have you been practicing the new defensive formation since last week?"', 'Change the direct speech above into reported speech!', '[{"key":"A","text":"Coach Ryan asked his players that they had been practicing the new defensive formation since the previous week."},{"key":"B","text":"Coach Ryan asked his players whether they were practicing the new defensive formation since last week."},{"key":"C","text":"Coach Ryan asked his players whether they have been practicing the new defensive formation since the previous week."},{"key":"D","text":"Coach Ryan asked his players whether we had been practicing the new defensive formation since last week."},{"key":"E","text":"Coach Ryan asked his players whether they had been practicing the new defensive formation since the previous week."}]'::jsonb, 'E', 'For Yes/No questions, use "whether" (not "that"), adjust "you -> they", backshift "have been practicing -> had been practicing," and shift "last week."', 'Yes/No questions take "whether/if"; "have been practicing" shifts to "had been practicing," "you" becomes "they," and "last week" becomes "the previous week."', ARRAY['reported-speech', 'yes-no-question', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-034', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'mudah', 'C2', 'text', 'Mrs. Lin reminded us, "Don''t forget to submit your research proposals before Friday."', 'Change the direct speech above into reported speech!', '[{"key":"A","text":"Mrs. Lin reminded us not to forget to submit their research proposals before Friday."},{"key":"B","text":"Mrs. Lin reminded us not to forget to submit our research proposals before Friday."},{"key":"C","text":"Mrs. Lin reminded us to not forget to submit our research proposals before Friday."},{"key":"D","text":"Mrs. Lin reminded us don''t forget to submit our research proposals before Friday."},{"key":"E","text":"Mrs. Lin reminds us not to forget to submit your research proposals before Friday."}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Negative command "Don''t forget" -> "not to forget," and "us ... your" -> "us ... our."', '"Reminded us" pairs with negative infinitive "not to forget," and addressing "us" changes "your" to "our."', ARRAY['reported-speech', 'negative-imperative', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-035', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'Reported speech: Mr. Aris said that he had been teaching astrophysics for fifteen years.
Direct speech: Mr. Aris said, "I … astrophysics for fifteen years."', 'The correct verb phrase to complete the direct speech is ….', '[{"key":"A","text":"have been teaching"},{"key":"B","text":"am teaching"},{"key":"C","text":"was teaching"},{"key":"D","text":"had taught"},{"key":"E","text":"has been teaching"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'What Present Perfect Continuous form with "I" and "for fifteen years" backshifts to "had been teaching"?', 'Restoring Past Perfect Continuous ("had been teaching") with ongoing duration ("for fifteen years") gives Present Perfect Continuous with subject "I": "have been teaching."', ARRAY['reported-to-direct', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-036', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'mudah', 'C2', 'text', 'Reported speech: Clara mentioned that her team had won the national robotics trophy the previous year.
Direct speech: Clara mentioned, "My team … the national robotics trophy last year."', 'The correct verb to complete the direct speech is ….', '[{"key":"A","text":"won"},{"key":"B","text":"has won"},{"key":"C","text":"had won"},{"key":"D","text":"was winning"},{"key":"E","text":"wins"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Look at the direct speech time clue "last year."', 'Because the direct quote includes "last year," the original verb was Simple Past ("won"), which backshifted to "had won" in reported speech.', ARRAY['reported-to-direct', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-037', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'Ms. Bima asked the class, "Are you preparing your slides for the science seminar right now?"', 'Which sentence accurately converts Ms. Bima’s question into reported speech?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Ms. Bima asked the class whether we are preparing our slides for the science seminar then."},{"key":"B","text":"Ms. Bima asked the class whether were they preparing their slides for the science seminar right now."},{"key":"C","text":"Ms. Bima asked the class whether they were preparing their slides for the science seminar then."},{"key":"D","text":"Ms. Bima asked the class if are they preparing their slides for the science seminar at that moment."},{"key":"E","text":"Ms. Bima asked the class that they prepared their slides for the science seminar then."}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'Adjust four things: "whether/if", "you/your -> they/their", "are preparing -> were preparing", and "right now -> then/at that moment."', 'Statement word order ("they were preparing") follows "whether," pronouns shift for "the class" ("they/their"), and "right now" becomes "then."', ARRAY['reported-speech', 'yes-no-question', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-038', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'sulit', 'C4', 'text', 'Evelyn says, "My sister was practicing the violin at 7:00 PM last night."', 'Which sentence correctly converts Evelyn’s statement into reported speech?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Evelyn says whether her sister was practicing the violin at 7:00 PM last night."},{"key":"B","text":"Evelyn says that her sister is practicing the violin at 7:00 PM last night."},{"key":"C","text":"Evelyn says that her sister was practicing the violin at 7:00 PM last night."},{"key":"D","text":"Evelyn said that my sister was practicing the violin at 7:00 PM last night."},{"key":"E","text":"Evelyn says that her sister had been practicing the violin at 7:00 PM the night before."}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'Watch the reporting verb "says" — present tense reporting keeps the verb tense and time phrase unchanged!', 'Because "says" is Simple Present, "was practicing" and "last night" do NOT backshift; only the possessive pronoun shifts from "My" to "her."', ARRAY['reported-speech', 'present-reporting', 'hots', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-039', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'Reported speech: Liam said that he had submitted his scholarship application two days before.', 'Which direct speech sentence corresponds accurately to the reported sentence above?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Liam said, \"I submitted my scholarship application two days ago.\""},{"key":"B","text":"Liam said, \"I have submitted his scholarship application two days before.\""},{"key":"C","text":"Liam said, \"He submitted my scholarship application two days ago.\""},{"key":"D","text":"Liam said, \"I was submitting my scholarship application two days ago.\""},{"key":"E","text":"Liam says, \"I had submitted my scholarship application two days ago.\""}]'::jsonb, 'A', '"Two days before" restores to "two days ago," which requires Simple Past ("submitted").', 'Converting back from "had submitted ... two days before" yields "I submitted my scholarship application two days ago."', ARRAY['reported-to-direct', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-040', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'medium', 'C3', 'none', NULL, 'Fill in the blank with the correct verb!
Direct speech: The biology teacher explained, "Plants convert sunlight into chemical energy through photosynthesis."
Reported speech: The biology teacher explained that plants … sunlight into chemical energy through photosynthesis.', '[{"key":"A","text":"would convert"},{"key":"B","text":"are converting"},{"key":"C","text":"convert"},{"key":"D","text":"had converted"},{"key":"E","text":"were converting"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'Consider what happens to universal scientific facts in reported speech.', 'Scientific laws and general truths remain in Simple Present ("convert") even after a past reporting verb ("explained").', ARRAY['reported-speech', 'general-truth']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-041', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'medium', 'C3', 'none', NULL, 'Fill in the blank with the correct modal!
Direct speech: The museum curator told us, "You must show your student badges at the archive desk."
Reported speech: The museum curator told us that we … our student badges at the archive desk.', '[{"key":"A","text":"have to show"},{"key":"B","text":"could showing"},{"key":"C","text":"might show"},{"key":"D","text":"had to show"},{"key":"E","text":"must showed"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Obligation modal "must" typically backshifts to past obligation "had to + V1" after "told."', 'In reported statements after a past verb ("told"), "must" (expressing obligation) changes to "had to show."', ARRAY['reported-speech', 'modal-backshift']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-042', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'medium', 'C3', 'none', NULL, 'Fill in the blank with the correct verb!
Direct speech: Hannah said to Ben, "I may volunteer at the city shelter tomorrow."
Reported speech: Hannah told Ben that she … at the city shelter the next day.', '[{"key":"A","text":"had volunteered"},{"key":"B","text":"might volunteer"},{"key":"C","text":"must volunteer"},{"key":"D","text":"will volunteer"},{"key":"E","text":"may volunteered"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Modal "may" backshifts to "might" + base verb when reported with "told."', 'Modal "may" shifts to "might" ("might volunteer") and "tomorrow" changes to "the next day."', ARRAY['reported-speech', 'modal-backshift']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-043', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'sulit', 'C4', 'none', NULL, 'Direct speech: The park ranger warned the campers, "Never leave open food outside your tents at night!"
Which sentence correctly converts the warning into reported speech?', '[{"key":"A","text":"The park ranger warned the campers never to leave open food outside their tents at night."},{"key":"B","text":"The park ranger warned the campers leaving not open food outside their tents at night."},{"key":"C","text":"The park ranger warned the campers to never left open food outside their tents at night."},{"key":"D","text":"The park ranger warned the campers that never leave open food outside your tents at night."},{"key":"E","text":"The park ranger warned the campers did not leave open food outside their tents at night."}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Negative imperatives with "Never..." become "warned + object + never to + V1," updating "your" to "their."', '"Never leave..." transitions to "never to leave" (base verb after "to"), and "your tents" changes to "their tents" for "the campers."', ARRAY['reported-speech', 'negative-imperative', 'hots']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-044', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'sulit', 'C4', 'none', NULL, 'Direct speech: Olivia asked her brother, "Who wrote this handwritten letter on the kitchen table?"
Which reported speech version is grammatically accurate?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Olivia asked her brother who has written this handwritten letter on the kitchen table."},{"key":"B","text":"Olivia asked her brother whether who had written that handwritten letter on the kitchen table."},{"key":"C","text":"Olivia asked her brother who had written this handwritten letter on the kitchen table."},{"key":"D","text":"Olivia asked her brother who had written that handwritten letter on the kitchen table."},{"key":"E","text":"Olivia asked her brother who wrote did that handwritten letter on the kitchen table."}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Check three details: "who" needs no "whether," Simple Past ("wrote") backshifts to Past Perfect ("had written"), and "this" shifts to "that."', 'Subject WH-questions keep "who" directly without "whether/if"; "wrote" backshifts to "had written"; "this" converts to "that."', ARRAY['reported-speech', 'wh-question', 'deictic-shift', 'hots']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-045', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'medium', 'C3', 'none', NULL, 'Direct speech: Leo promised Maya, "I will bring back your physics textbook tonight."
Change the direct speech above into reported speech!', '[{"key":"A","text":"Leo promised Maya that I would bring back her physics textbook tonight."},{"key":"B","text":"Leo promised Maya that he would bring back her physics textbook that night."},{"key":"C","text":"Leo promised Maya that he will bring back her physics textbook tonight."},{"key":"D","text":"Leo promised Maya that he would brought back your physics textbook that night."},{"key":"E","text":"Leo promised Maya that he would bring back his physics textbook that night."}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Shift "I -> he", "will -> would", "your (Maya''s) -> her", and "tonight -> that night."', 'Past reporting "promised" turns "will bring" into "would bring," "your" (referring to Maya) into "her," and "tonight" into "that night."', ARRAY['reported-speech', 'modal-backshift', 'time-shift']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-046', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'sulit', 'C4', 'none', NULL, 'Reported speech: Kevin wanted to know how long we had been waiting outside the clinic.
Convert this sentence accurately into direct speech!', '[{"key":"A","text":"Kevin wanted to know, \"How long had we been waiting outside the clinic?\""},{"key":"B","text":"Kevin wanted to know, \"How long are we waiting outside the clinic?\""},{"key":"C","text":"Kevin wanted to know, \"How long you have been waiting outside the clinic?\""},{"key":"D","text":"Kevin wanted to know, \"How long did you waited outside the clinic?\""},{"key":"E","text":"Kevin wanted to know, \"How long have you been waiting outside the clinic?\""}]'::jsonb, 'E', 'Revert "we had been waiting" (after past "wanted") to a direct question addressed to "you" using Present Perfect Continuous.', 'When Kevin directly asked the group ("you"), he asked "How long have you been waiting...?", which backshifted to "we had been waiting" when reported by them.', ARRAY['reported-to-direct', 'wh-question', 'hots']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-047', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'medium', 'C3', 'none', NULL, 'Direct speech: The receptionist asked the guest, "Could you fill out this registration form with a black pen?"
Which indirect speech option properly reports this polite request?', '[{"key":"A","text":"The receptionist told to the guest fill out that registration form with a black pen."},{"key":"B","text":"The receptionist asked the guest to fill out that registration form with a black pen."},{"key":"C","text":"The receptionist asked the guest that he fills out this registration form with a black pen."},{"key":"D","text":"The receptionist asked the guest if did he fill out this registration form with a black pen."},{"key":"E","text":"The receptionist asked the guest filling out that registration form with a black pen."}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Polite requests framed as "Could you + V1...?" often report cleanly as "asked + object + to-infinitive."', '"Could you fill out..." expresses a polite request, properly reported as "asked the guest to fill out that registration form..." (shifting "this" to "that").', ARRAY['reported-speech', 'polite-request']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-048', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'sulit', 'C4', 'none', NULL, 'Reported speech: The principal reminded the finalists that they should check their microphones before stepping onto the stage.
Which direct quote matches this reported sentence?', '[{"key":"A","text":"The principal reminded the finalists, \"We shall check my microphones before stepping onto the stage.\""},{"key":"B","text":"The principal reminded the finalists, \"They should checked their microphones before stepping onto the stage.\""},{"key":"C","text":"The principal reminded the finalists, \"Should you checking your microphones before stepping onto the stage.\""},{"key":"D","text":"The principal reminded the finalists, \"You should check your microphones before stepping onto the stage.\""},{"key":"E","text":"The principal reminds the finalists, \"You would check their microphones before stepping onto the stage.\""}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Modal "should" stays unchanged in reported speech; restore "they/their" back to "you/your" spoken directly to the finalists.', '"Should" does not backshift, so direct speech used "You should check your microphones..." when addressing the finalists.', ARRAY['reported-to-direct', 'modal-no-backshift', 'hots']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-049', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'medium', 'C3', 'none', NULL, 'Direct speech: Nadia told Farhan, "I didn''t see anyone near the science lab twenty minutes ago."
Change the sentence above into reported speech!', '[{"key":"A","text":"Nadia told Farhan that she didn’t saw anyone near the science lab twenty minutes earlier."},{"key":"B","text":"Nadia told Farhan whether she hadn’t seen anyone near the science lab twenty minutes before."},{"key":"C","text":"Nadia said Farhan that she hadn’t seen anyone near the science lab twenty minutes ago."},{"key":"D","text":"Nadia told Farhan that she hasn’t seen anyone near the science lab twenty minutes ago."},{"key":"E","text":"Nadia told Farhan that she hadn’t seen anyone near the science lab twenty minutes before."}]'::jsonb, 'E', 'Check "didn''t see -> hadn''t seen" AND "... ago -> ... before/earlier." Also remember "told" takes an object directly without "whether" for statements.', 'Under past "told," negative Simple Past ("didn’t see") shifts to negative Past Perfect ("hadn’t seen"), and "ago" converts to "before."', ARRAY['reported-speech', 'simple-past-backshift', 'time-shift']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-RS-050', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'reported-speech', 'Reported Speech & Direct Speech', 'sulit', 'C5', 'none', NULL, 'Direct speech: "Have you ever visited the ancient caves in Maros, Dina?" Riko will ask.
How should this future-tense reporting clause be written in reported speech?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Riko will ask Dina whether she has ever visited the ancient caves in Maros."},{"key":"B","text":"Riko would ask Dina whether did she ever visit the ancient caves in Maros."},{"key":"C","text":"Riko will ask Dina that she has ever visited the ancient caves in Maros."},{"key":"D","text":"Riko will ask Dina whether she had ever visited the ancient caves in Maros."},{"key":"E","text":"Riko will ask Dina whether has she ever visited the ancient caves in Maros."}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Just like Present Tense reporting verbs, Future Tense reporting verbs ("will ask") cause NO tense backshift.', 'When the reporting verb is Future ("will ask"), Present Perfect ("Have you ever visited") does NOT shift to Past Perfect—it remains Present Perfect ("whether she has ever visited").', ARRAY['reported-speech', 'future-reporting', 'hots']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-001', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'mudah', 'C2', 'text', 'Next week, our school will host an international cultural exchange fair in the auditorium. Many guests from partner schools will visit our booths. Therefore, … when greeting the visitors and explaining our local traditions. Stand tall, make eye contact, and speak clearly.', 'Which is the correct imperative form to complete the paragraph above?', '[{"key":"A","text":"You are polite"},{"key":"B","text":"Must be polite"},{"key":"C","text":"Be polite"},{"key":"D","text":"Being polite"},{"key":"E","text":"To be polite"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'An imperative sentence with an adjective ("polite") starts directly with the bare infinitive "Be."', 'Imperatives using adjectives use the base verb "Be" without a subject ("Be polite"), matching "Stand tall, make eye contact, and speak clearly."', ARRAY['imperatives', 'positive-imperative', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-002', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'mudah', 'C2', 'text', 'Hiking in a national park is an exhilarating outdoor activity. While walking along the forest trail, … plastic wrappers or bottles on the ground because litter harms local wildlife. In addition, … on the marked wooden pathways so you do not damage rare plants.', 'Which is the correct imperative form to complete the paragraph above?', '[{"key":"A","text":"don''t leaving – stayed"},{"key":"B","text":"no leaving – you stay"},{"key":"C","text":"not leave – staying"},{"key":"D","text":"do not leave – stay"},{"key":"E","text":"to not leave – to stay"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Negative imperatives take "do not + V1", while positive imperatives take bare "V1".', 'Use "do not leave" for the negative command and the base verb "stay" for the positive command.', ARRAY['imperatives', 'negative-imperative', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-003', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'medium', 'C3', 'html', 'Last Sunday afternoon, my cousins and I visited the city planetarium. We explored the space exhibition and touched a real meteorite. <u class="eng-underline">At three o''clock</u>, we entered the dome theater to watch a documentary about black holes. Afterward, we bought space-themed souvenirs at the gift shop.', 'Which question correctly asks for the underlined information?', '[{"key":"A","text":"What did you do inside the dome theater at three o’clock?"},{"key":"B","text":"When did you enter the dome theater to watch a documentary?"},{"key":"C","text":"When do you enter the dome theater to watch a documentary?"},{"key":"D","text":"Where did you enter the dome theater to watch a documentary?"},{"key":"E","text":"Who entered the dome theater with you last Sunday afternoon?"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '"At three o''clock" is a time phrase ("When"), and the action occurred "Last Sunday afternoon" (Simple Past auxiliary "did").', '"At three o’clock" specifies time ("When"), and Simple Past requires auxiliary "did" + base verb "enter."', ARRAY['wh-questions', 'simple-past', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-004', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'medium', 'C3', 'html', 'Kevin is organizing his studio desk for an upcoming illustration commission. He wants all his art supplies within easy reach. He has arranged <u class="eng-underline">two dozen watercolor brushes</u> inside a ceramic jar. He is excited to start painting the book cover tonight.', 'Which question correctly asks for the underlined information?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Where has Kevin arranged two dozen watercolor brushes?"},{"key":"B","text":"Who has arranged two dozen watercolor brushes in a jar?"},{"key":"C","text":"What has Kevin arranged inside a ceramic jar?"},{"key":"D","text":"Why has Kevin arranged two dozen watercolor brushes?"},{"key":"E","text":"When has Kevin arranged two dozen watercolor brushes?"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '"Two dozen watercolor brushes" is the object ("What"), and the sentence uses Present Perfect ("has arranged").', 'Asking for the object ("two dozen watercolor brushes") uses "What" while preserving Present Perfect inversion ("has Kevin arranged").', ARRAY['wh-questions', 'present-perfect', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-005', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'mudah', 'C2', 'text', 'Look at the indoor swimming pool during the morning training session right now. Several coaches are standing beside the lanes holding stopwatches.
…
Yes, the varsity swimmers are practicing their butterfly strokes. Their teammates are encouraging them from the poolside.', 'Which question correctly completes the dialogue above?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Do the varsity swimmers practice their butterfly strokes?"},{"key":"B","text":"Can the varsity swimmers practice their butterfly strokes?"},{"key":"C","text":"Have the varsity swimmers practiced their butterfly strokes?"},{"key":"D","text":"Are the varsity swimmers practicing their butterfly strokes?"},{"key":"E","text":"Did the varsity swimmers practice their butterfly strokes?"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Match both tense ("are practicing") and affirmative reply structure.', 'The reply "Yes, the varsity swimmers are practicing..." confirms a Present Continuous Yes/No question starting with "Are the varsity swimmers practicing...?".', ARRAY['yes-no-questions', 'present-continuous', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-006', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'medium', 'C3', 'html', 'Desert cacti survive prolonged droughts <u class="eng-underline">by storing large amounts of water inside their thick stems</u>.', 'Which question uses the underlined phrase above as its exact answer?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Why do desert cacti store large amounts of water?"},{"key":"B","text":"What do desert cacti avoid during dry winter months?"},{"key":"C","text":"When did desert cacti store large amounts of water?"},{"key":"D","text":"Where do desert cacti grow during prolonged droughts?"},{"key":"E","text":"How do desert cacti survive prolonged droughts?"}]'::jsonb, 'E', '"By + V-ing" answers a question about method or manner ("How"). Notice plural Simple Present "survive."', 'Prepositional phrases starting with "by + V-ing" explain method ("How"), and Simple Present plural "desert cacti" uses auxiliary "do" + V1 ("survive").', ARRAY['wh-questions', 'simple-present', 'hots', 'sas-x']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-007', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'mudah', 'C2', 'text', 'When transferring fragile antique manuscripts inside the school archive room, … cotton gloves first so natural skin oils do not stain the paper.', 'Which imperative form correctly completes the instruction?', '[{"key":"A","text":"put on"},{"key":"B","text":"putting on"},{"key":"C","text":"you putting on"},{"key":"D","text":"to put on"},{"key":"E","text":"puts on"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Direct procedural commands start with a base verb (V1).', 'Positive imperatives use the bare infinitive without "to" or -s/-ing endings: "put on."', ARRAY['imperatives', 'positive-imperative']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-008', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'mudah', 'C2', 'text', 'When thunder echoes across the soccer field during afternoon practice, … under tall isolated metal flagpoles, and … calmly into the brick gymnasium building.', 'Which imperative pair accurately completes the safety rule?', '[{"key":"A","text":"to not stand – walked"},{"key":"B","text":"do not stand – walk"},{"key":"C","text":"not standing – walking"},{"key":"D","text":"no stand – to walk"},{"key":"E","text":"does not stand – walks"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'First warn against standing under flagpoles ("do not + V1"), then tell students calmly to enter ("V1").', 'Negative command "do not stand" followed by affirmative command "walk" keeps parallel imperative structure.', ARRAY['imperatives', 'negative-imperative']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-009', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'mudah', 'C2', 'text', 'Public speaking beginners often speak far too quickly when nervous. Therefore, … a deep breath before beginning your presentation, and … afraid to pause briefly after key statistics.', 'Which imperative pair best completes the advice?', '[{"key":"A","text":"taking – are not"},{"key":"B","text":"take – do not be"},{"key":"C","text":"takes – be not to"},{"key":"D","text":"took – never to be"},{"key":"E","text":"to take – not be"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'For negative imperatives with adjective "afraid," place "do not" before "be."', 'Use base verb "take" for the first action and "do not be" before the adjective "afraid."', ARRAY['imperatives', 'be-imperative']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-010', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'To brew crisp pour-over coffee cleanly, … boiling water slowly in circular motion over the grounds, and … the paper filter until all water finishes dripping.', 'Which imperative pair accurately completes the brewing steps?', '[{"key":"A","text":"pours – not lift"},{"key":"B","text":"to pour – don’t to lift"},{"key":"C","text":"poured – never lifted"},{"key":"D","text":"pouring – do not lifting"},{"key":"E","text":"pour – do not lift"}]'::jsonb, 'E', 'Instructions require bare V1 ("pour") and "do not + V1" ("do not lift").', 'Imperative recipes use direct base verbs ("pour") and "do not + base verb" ("do not lift").', ARRAY['imperatives', 'procedure']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-011', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'When working near active 3D-printer nozzles in the engineering lab, … careful not to touch hot aluminum beds, and always … protective heat-resistant gloves when removing finished models.', 'Which imperative verb pair accurately completes both safety rules?', '[{"key":"A","text":"are – wearing"},{"key":"B","text":"being – wears"},{"key":"C","text":"must – must wear"},{"key":"D","text":"be – wear"},{"key":"E","text":"to be – to wear"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Adjective imperatives ("___ careful") require the bare infinitive "be," paired with base verb "wear."', 'In direct imperative instructions, adjectives take bare "be" ("be careful") and actions take V1 ("wear").', ARRAY['imperatives', 'be-imperative']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-012', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'Before locking the chemistry lab after fifth period, remember the closing checklist: … every Bunsen burner valve tightly, and … used beakers unwashed inside the sink.', 'Which imperative pair correctly completes the laboratory checklist?', '[{"key":"A","text":"shut off – never leave"},{"key":"B","text":"shut off – never to leave"},{"key":"C","text":"shuts off – did not leave"},{"key":"D","text":"to shut off – do not leaving"},{"key":"E","text":"shutting off – not leave"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Both "shut off" (V1) and "never leave" ("never + V1") form standard direct commands.', 'Positive imperative uses "shut off," and strong negative imperative uses "never + bare infinitive" ("never leave").', ARRAY['imperatives', 'negative-imperative']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-013', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'sulit', 'C4', 'text', 'Read these five sign notices posted at a botanical park:
1. Please do not feed the wild monkeys along the bridge.
2. Visitors to keep quiet inside the butterfly greenhouse.
3. Let us check the weather forecast before climbing.
4. Always wearing life jackets when kayaking on the lake.
5. Never pick rare orchids from the forest floor.', 'Which notice number contains a grammatical error in its imperative structure?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Notice 3 (\"Let us check...\") and Notice 5 (\"Never pick...\")"},{"key":"B","text":"Notice 1 and Notice 2 only"},{"key":"C","text":"Notice 1 (\"Please do not feed...\") and Notice 5 (\"Never pick...\")"},{"key":"D","text":"Notice 1 (\"Please do not feed...\") and Notice 3 (\"Let us check...\")"},{"key":"E","text":"Notice 2 (\"Visitors to keep...\") and Notice 4 (\"Always wearing...\")"}]'::jsonb, 'E', 'Imperatives never use "to + V1" without a subject verb or standalone "-ing" verbs ("wearing").', 'Notice 2 wrongly puts a bare to-infinitive ("Visitors to keep") instead of "Keep quiet," and Notice 4 uses "-ing" ("wearing") instead of bare "Always wear."', ARRAY['imperatives', 'error-analysis', 'hots']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-014', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'When installing software updates on school Chromebooks, … patient if the progress bar pauses at eighty percent, and … the power button mid-installation.', 'Which imperative pair accurately completes the IT guide?', '[{"key":"A","text":"be – do not press"},{"key":"B","text":"being – never pressing"},{"key":"C","text":"keep being – don’t pressing"},{"key":"D","text":"to be – not to press"},{"key":"E","text":"are – should not press"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Pair adjective "patient" with "Be" and prohibit pressing the button with "do not + V1."', '"Be patient" uses base "be" + adjective, and "do not press" provides the negative command.', ARRAY['imperatives', 'be-imperative', 'negative-imperative']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-015', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'sulit', 'C4', 'html', '<u class="eng-underline">Two Grade 10 biology students</u> discovered an unusual bioluminescent mushroom behind the school greenhouse yesterday.', 'Which WH-question correctly asks for the underlined subject?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Who was discovered an unusual bioluminescent mushroom behind the school greenhouse yesterday?"},{"key":"B","text":"Who did discover an unusual bioluminescent mushroom behind the school greenhouse yesterday?"},{"key":"C","text":"Whom discovered an unusual bioluminescent mushroom behind the school greenhouse yesterday?"},{"key":"D","text":"Who discovered an unusual bioluminescent mushroom behind the school greenhouse yesterday?"},{"key":"E","text":"Which discovered an unusual bioluminescent mushroom behind the school greenhouse yesterday?"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'When asking about the SUBJECT of a Simple Past verb, do NOT add the auxiliary "did"—put "Who" straight before the V2 verb.', 'Subject questions omit do/does/did auxiliaries: "Who discovered ...?" directly replaces the subject phrase.', ARRAY['wh-questions', 'subject-question', 'hots']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-016', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'medium', 'C3', 'html', 'Dr. Ratna has been mentoring the national physics Olympiad squad <u class="eng-underline">for six consecutive months</u>.', 'Which question accurately asks for the underlined duration?', '[{"key":"A","text":"When has Dr. Ratna been mentoring the national physics Olympiad squad?"},{"key":"B","text":"How many times has Dr. Ratna been mentoring the national physics Olympiad squad?"},{"key":"C","text":"How long has Dr. Ratna been mentoring the national physics Olympiad squad?"},{"key":"D","text":"How long Dr. Ratna has been mentoring the national physics Olympiad squad?"},{"key":"E","text":"How often did Dr. Ratna mentor the national physics Olympiad squad?"}]'::jsonb, 'C', '"For six consecutive months" asks about time span ("How long"), and the verb uses Present Perfect Continuous inversion ("has Dr. Ratna been mentoring").', '"How long" targets duration ("for six months"), followed by inverted auxiliary "has Dr. Ratna been mentoring."', ARRAY['wh-questions', 'present-perfect-continuous']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-017', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'mudah', 'C2', 'html', 'The municipal water agency tests reservoir samples <u class="eng-underline">twice every week</u> to verify drinking safety.', 'Which question accurately asks for the underlined frequency?', '[{"key":"A","text":"How often tests the municipal water agency reservoir samples?"},{"key":"B","text":"How long does the municipal water agency test reservoir samples?"},{"key":"C","text":"When did the municipal water agency test reservoir samples?"},{"key":"D","text":"How many does the municipal water agency test reservoir samples?"},{"key":"E","text":"How often does the municipal water agency test reservoir samples?"}]'::jsonb, 'E', '"Twice every week" asks about frequency ("How often"), and singular Simple Present takes "does ... test."', 'Frequency expressions like "twice every week" answer "How often," inverted with "does" + base verb "test."', ARRAY['wh-questions', 'simple-present']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-018', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'medium', 'C3', 'html', 'The student filmmakers stayed late at the auditorium <u class="eng-underline">because the stage spotlights needed recalibration</u>.', 'Which question accurately asks for the underlined reason?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Why did the student filmmakers stay late at the auditorium?"},{"key":"B","text":"How did the student filmmakers stay late at the auditorium?"},{"key":"C","text":"Why were the student filmmakers stay late at the auditorium?"},{"key":"D","text":"Why do the student filmmakers stayed late at the auditorium?"},{"key":"E","text":"What did the student filmmakers stay late at the auditorium?"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'Clauses starting with "because..." answer "Why," and past verb "stayed" takes "did + stay."', '"Why" asks for the reason, paired properly with Simple Past "did ... stay."', ARRAY['wh-questions', 'simple-past']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-019', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'medium', 'C3', 'html', 'Volunteers planted <u class="eng-underline">three hundred mangrove saplings</u> along the northern lagoon yesterday morning.', 'Which question accurately asks for the underlined countable quantity?', '[{"key":"A","text":"How many mangrove saplings volunteers planted along the northern lagoon yesterday morning?"},{"key":"B","text":"How many mangrove saplings did volunteers plant along the northern lagoon yesterday morning?"},{"key":"C","text":"How much mangrove saplings did volunteers plant along the northern lagoon yesterday morning?"},{"key":"D","text":"What many mangrove saplings did volunteers plant along the northern lagoon yesterday morning?"},{"key":"E","text":"How long did volunteers plant mangrove saplings along the northern lagoon yesterday morning?"}]'::jsonb, 'B', '"Saplings" is plural countable ("How many"), followed by past auxiliary "did" + V1 ("plant").', 'Use "How many" with plural countable nouns ("saplings"), then invert "did volunteers plant."', ARRAY['wh-questions', 'quantifiers', 'simple-past']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-020', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'sulit', 'C4', 'html', 'Coach Bima accidentally picked up <u class="eng-underline">Tari''s</u> bright orange stopwatch near the track bench.', 'Which question asks specifically for the underlined possessive owner?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Whose bright orange stopwatch did Coach Bima accidentally pick up near the track bench?"},{"key":"B","text":"Whose bright orange stopwatch Coach Bima picked up near the track bench?"},{"key":"C","text":"Which Coach Bima accidentally picked up bright orange stopwatch near the track bench?"},{"key":"D","text":"Whom bright orange stopwatch did Coach Bima accidentally pick up near the track bench?"},{"key":"E","text":"Who bright orange stopwatch did Coach Bima accidentally pick up near the track bench?"}]'::jsonb, 'A', 'To ask about ownership ("Tari''s"), use "Whose + noun phrase" followed by "did Coach Bima ... pick up."', '"Whose + noun" asks about possession, and past object questions invert with "did" + bare infinitive "pick up."', ARRAY['wh-questions', 'possessive', 'hots']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-021', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'mudah', 'C2', 'html', 'The astronomy club will set up three solar telescopes <u class="eng-underline">on the school rooftop observatory</u> tomorrow morning.', 'Which question asks for the underlined location?', '[{"key":"A","text":"What will the astronomy club set up on the rooftop tomorrow morning?"},{"key":"B","text":"When will the astronomy club set up three solar telescopes tomorrow morning?"},{"key":"C","text":"Where does the astronomy club setting up three solar telescopes tomorrow morning?"},{"key":"D","text":"Where the astronomy club will set up three solar telescopes tomorrow morning?"},{"key":"E","text":"Where will the astronomy club set up three solar telescopes tomorrow morning?"}]'::jsonb, 'E', '"On the school rooftop observatory" answers "Where" with future modal inversion ("will the astronomy club set up").', 'Location questions begin with "Where" and invert the modal "will" before the subject ("will the astronomy club set up").', ARRAY['wh-questions', 'future-will']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-022', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'sulit', 'C4', 'html', 'The robotics mentor handed the bronze medal <u class="eng-underline">to our team captain</u> after the final run.', 'Which question asks for the underlined recipient in correct standard English?', '[{"key":"A","text":"What did the robotics mentor hand to our team captain after the final run?"},{"key":"B","text":"Whose did the robotics mentor hand the bronze medal after the final run?"},{"key":"C","text":"Who did the robotics mentor hand the bronze medal to after the final run?"},{"key":"D","text":"Who handed the robotics mentor the bronze medal after the final run?"},{"key":"E","text":"Whom handed the bronze medal to our team captain after the final run?"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'Here "our team captain" is the object of the preposition "to," NOT the subject—so keep "did" + V1 ("hand") and retain "to."', 'Object-of-preposition question keeps "to" at the end with inverted past auxiliary: "Who (or Whom) did the robotics mentor hand the bronze medal to...?".', ARRAY['wh-questions', 'object-question', 'hots']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-023', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'mudah', 'C2', 'text', 'Noah: I heard the archaeology club went to Sangiran last weekend.
…
Tara: Yes, they examined several fossil exhibits inside the museum pavilion.', 'Which Yes/No question correctly completes Noah’s turn?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Do they examine fossil exhibits inside the museum last weekend?"},{"key":"B","text":"Were they visit the museum displays inside Sangiran last weekend?"},{"key":"C","text":"Did they found the trip informative and visited the museum displays?"},{"key":"D","text":"Did they find the trip informative and visit the museum displays?"},{"key":"E","text":"Have they examined the museum displays last weekend?"}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'Use "Did + subject + base verb (V1)" for a past Yes/No question.', 'Simple Past questions start with "Did" followed by base verbs ("find" and "visit"), never V2.', ARRAY['yes-no-questions', 'simple-past']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-024', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'Farah: You look relieved holding that thick folder.
…
Rendra: Yes, I have already submitted my complete scholarship essay to the registrar.', 'Which Yes/No question logically leads to Rendra’s reply?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Are you submit your complete scholarship essay yet?"},{"key":"B","text":"Did you have submitted your complete scholarship essay yet?"},{"key":"C","text":"Have you submitted your complete scholarship essay yet?"},{"key":"D","text":"Do you already submitted your complete scholarship essay?"},{"key":"E","text":"Had you submit your complete scholarship essay right now?"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'Match Present Perfect ("have already submitted") with Present Perfect question inversion using "yet."', 'Rendra answers using "have already submitted," matching "Have you submitted ... yet?".', ARRAY['yes-no-questions', 'present-perfect']::text[]),
  ('ENG10-IQ-025', 'Bahasa Inggris Kelas X', 'imperatives-questions', 'Imperatives & Question Formation', 'medium', 'C3', 'text', 'Officer: We noticed the auditorium roof leaking during yesterday’s storm.
…
Janitor: No, nobody was rehearsing inside when the rain broke the skylight.', 'Which Yes/No question accurately prompts the janitor’s response?', '[{"key":"A","text":"Is anyone rehearsed inside the auditorium yesterday during the storm?"},{"key":"B","text":"Was anyone rehearsing inside the auditorium when the rain broke the skylight?"},{"key":"C","text":"Does anyone rehearse inside the auditorium during yesterday’s storm?"},{"key":"D","text":"Had anyone was rehearsing inside the auditorium when the rain broke the skylight?"},{"key":"E","text":"Did anyone rehearsing inside the auditorium when the rain broke the skylight?"}]'::jsonb, 'B', 'Match Past Continuous ("nobody was rehearsing") with "Was + singular pronoun anyone + V-ing."', 'Past Continuous Yes/No questions invert "was" before "anyone" ("Was anyone rehearsing..."), matching "No, nobody was rehearsing...".', ARRAY['yes-no-questions', 'past-continuous']::text[])
